# Cursor AI Analysis Configuration — shortstoryfun

## Purpose
- Private single-user drafting tool. Raw drafts only — never present output as finished.
- Author approves premise and outline before any prose is drafted.

## Model Configuration
- **Provider**: OpenRouter only (`https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`), via `OpenAICompatibleProvider`
- **No local models**: no Ollama, no GPU, no on-device inference
- **Env (never hardcode model slugs in call sites)**:
  - `DRAFT_MODEL` default `qwen/qwen3.8-27b` (alt: `deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash`)
  - `PREMIUM_MODEL` default `moonshotai/kimi-k3.1-pro` — only when user passes `--premium`
- **Factory**: `create_provider` / `get_default_provider` in `src/shortstory/providers/`
- **Interface**: `BaseProvider.generate(system, prompt, temperature, max_tokens) -> GenerateResult`

## Pipeline
- Stages: spark → premise (checkpoint) → outline (checkpoint) → scene draft → quality → continuity → assemble
- Frameworks: story_circle, try_fail, mice
- Storage: `stories/<slug>/` Markdown + `provenance.jsonl` + `costs.jsonl`
- Prompts live in `prompts/*.md`

## Cost & Provenance
- Log tokens and $ cost every call; enforce `BUDGET_CAP_USD`
- Provenance JSONL per model call; `diff` reports % human-changed

## IP Safety
- Reject sparks naming living authors or franchises (`style/ip_gate.py`)
- Voice references only from author's `style.yaml`

## Interface
- CLI primary (`python -m src.shortstory.cli_app` / `cli_app.py`)
- Minimal local web UI: `webapp.py` on 127.0.0.1 only

## Testing
- pytest; mock provider only — never call a real model in tests

## Do not
- Add Redis/RQ, rate limits, gunicorn/Docker deploy, multi-user auth, or public hosting
- Auto-select premium model
- Fall back to formulaic template prose generators
